# Pairs with EventualConvergence. Reproduces production before #4599 (#4587): the fall-off
# probe reads only the receiver's own WAL, so a source trim past the receiver's
# cursor is never detected and no re-bootstrap is requested. The skipped entries
# reach the receiver by no path.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceTrimNeverRebootstraps
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a trim past the receiver requests no re-bootstrap, so the entries it skipped never arrive
PERTURBS: Trim

--- FIND
    /\ skipped' = (cursor[BootEdge] + 1)..Len(wal[BootSource])
    /\ requested' = TRUE
--- REPLACE
    /\ skipped' = (cursor[BootEdge] + 1)..Len(wal[BootSource])
\* MUTATION: nothing detects the fall-off.
    /\ requested' = requested
--- END
